{"data": [{"author_id": "800428109006704640", "created_at": "2026-11-09T23:22:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119933789338255697"], "id": "2119933789338255697", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1633874951508721686", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119883176726409645", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs wasn't this already present? My dot has been able to see my loal machines all along... 🧐", "url": "https://x.com/diablovoxx/status/2119933789338255697"}, {"author_id": "21273046", "created_at": "2026-11-09T23:20:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119933250579898601"], "id": "2119933250579898601", "in_reply_to_user_id": "384098551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119884573190545726", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_samirism Appreciate dots being able to spawn worktrees directly! I had my dot monitoring the situation and it just let me know about the improvement today!", "url": "https://x.com/adamalix/status/2119933250579898601"}, {"author_id": "1922667398206722049", "created_at": "2026-11-09T23:11:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119930802419253480"], "id": "2119930802419253480", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1605", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@sama and @steipete,\n\nYour models are great, and your apps have a strong foundation. Where I think there's the most room to grow is the user experience.\n\nThis may be a controversial take, but I don't really need more ways to text, call or Slack my Dot. What I'd love is for Dots", "url": "https://x.com/ProtomotaLab/status/2119930802419253480"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["16_2119928678159421440"]}, "author_id": "2093047415150448640", "created_at": "2026-11-09T23:02:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119928732425310505"], "id": "2119928732425310505", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 290, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Introducing /seo-manager-agent\n\nSend Grok Bot or ChatGPT Dots one message, and it becomes your full-time SEO manager.\n\nEvery Monday, see what moved and exactly what to fix.\n\nGet yours: https://t.co/bqMWFeoxFp\n\nSetup below 👇 https://t.co/iC47bNPULV", "url": "https://x.com/openseo/status/2119928732425310505"}, {"author_id": "1578958663", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:59:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119927862723817967"], "id": "2119927862723817967", "in_reply_to_user_id": "6204132", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119892902113427580", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@brandontroberts You can do that with ChatGPT Dots", "url": "https://x.com/ryan_ntk/status/2119927862723817967"}, {"author_id": "365858677", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:54:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119926680588624328"], "id": "2119926680588624328", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1633874951508721686", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119883176726409645", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs @OpenAI Dots suck @bot 10x better", "url": "https://x.com/Boston_Futures/status/2119926680588624328"}, {"author_id": "1083719964991852544", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:45:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119924429505622163"], "id": "2119924429505622163", "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 192, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119918987543032038", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@alexandr_wang I don’t even like Muse, and still this is a really cool win!\n\nI’m so jealous, I wish ChatGPT and my Dot had this!", "url": "https://x.com/MichaelM_117/status/2119924429505622163"}, {"author_id": "303417347", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:37:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119922325957079152"], "id": "2119922325957079152", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1633874951508721686", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 62, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119883189028266171", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs Unpopular opinion: OpenAI Dots is unusable.\nMe: Did you finish the task? Dots: Checking. Me: It’s been 10 minutes. Dots: Checking. Me: Are you okay? Dots: Checking. Me: Are you fucking dumb? Dots: Checking.\nGrok Bot and Muse actually do the work. This is just a cute blob", "url": "https://x.com/ZeroSpacePirate/status/2119922325957079152"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2119922037682479104"]}, "author_id": "1429827690773819395", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:36:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119922041889439838"], "id": "2119922041889439838", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Search “OpenAI Dots”\n\nSponsored Result: “Grok Bot Is Better” 😂 https://t.co/mTWXgg88an", "url": "https://x.com/ConnInvests/status/2119922041889439838"}, {"author_id": "3428512283", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:32:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119921037987205179"], "id": "2119921037987205179", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119864571733446774", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Had my dot checking every 5 minutes since the teaser yesterday. Had to have bought one of the first ones available. Cannot wait to get my hands on this! https://t.co/2tL0swfjrV", "url": "https://x.com/Matthewod11/status/2119921037987205179"}, {"author_id": "1414740038781333528", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:29:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119920453498310915"], "id": "2119920453498310915", "in_reply_to_user_id": "384098551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119884573190545726", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_samirism Fantastic this is a big update. I've also noticed my dot being more proactive without being asked which is a step in the right direction. \n\nAbility to create multiple dots for clear role and task separation next please 🙏", "url": "https://x.com/0x_Dela/status/2119920453498310915"}, {"author_id": "2056358179286429696", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:20:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119918174938485148"], "id": "2119918174938485148", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 49, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Which AI agent has the most potential?\n\n- Grok Bot\n- Claude Duet\n- Meta Muse\n- OpenAI Dots\n\n#AI #ArtificialIntelligence #AIAgents #Tech #MachineLearning #OpenAI #Claude #Grok #Meta", "url": "https://x.com/VhirtyStudio/status/2119918174938485148"}, {"author_id": "88933191", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:15:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119916895633633324"], "id": "2119916895633633324", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1873640046278144000", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119814772145451345", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@openanysi @Muse @bot @OpenAI @NousResearch for the self-hosted lane: i build kwant — team of AI bots in one binary, spaces, handoffs, routines, approvals. Mac/Linux/Windows/VPS, your keys or local models. open source alt to Grok Bot / Claude Duet / OpenAI dots\nhttps://t.co/6WgxXSNAF1", "url": "https://x.com/olekss/status/2119916895633633324"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2119916784027312128", "3_2119913204159520768", "3_2119916505705963521"]}, "author_id": "1175878265246031875", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:15:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119916799777194124"], "id": "2119916799777194124", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 254, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Setup script to sync my dot files using Chezmoi and install tools and applications from my previous PC using a Brewfile for batch installation. https://t.co/O7eYhSxTWG", "url": "https://x.com/obiabo_immanuel/status/2119916799777194124"}, {"author_id": "1326548955165908992", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:14:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119916650745286680"], "id": "2119916650745286680", "in_reply_to_user_id": "384098551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119884573190545726", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_samirism My dot can't even use 1 😂", "url": "https://x.com/systemwithin/status/2119916650745286680"}, {"author_id": "141607086", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:56:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119911986628849843"], "id": "2119911986628849843", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1674506538336022528", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119898209980203122", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@nickbaumann_ I'm hoping to set a \"pecking order\"  for my dot.\n1 Use the dots bot\n2 use my pc\n3 use the server i have the client installed on 24x7", "url": "https://x.com/jimmberry/status/2119911986628849843"}, {"author_id": "1884050482479652867", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:48:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119909970062008712"], "id": "2119909970062008712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Convenient Talk | After a Month, ChatGPT Dots Failed Me #Shorts https://t.co/owD1lWJknr via @YouTube", "url": "https://x.com/DenellD/status/2119909970062008712"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2119908739989782528"]}, "author_id": "1605309974476980225", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:47:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119909869423853592"], "id": "2119909869423853592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "I received a text from Instinct saying my AI assistant’s number had changed. I verified it through my account, but it raised an important security concern.\n\nWhat if an attacker sent a similar notice and redirected me to their own AI?\n\nUnlike traditional smishing, the attacker https://t.co/QYirVfXBZg", "url": "https://x.com/jer_mchugh/status/2119909869423853592"}, {"author_id": "1217165870", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:47:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119909711961289064"], "id": "2119909711961289064", "in_reply_to_user_id": "384098551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 125, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119884573190545726", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_samirism I can!t manage to make my dot manage a Linux PC is a skill issue or its not doable yet?", "url": "https://x.com/TulkasXBT/status/2119909711961289064"}, {"author_id": "90396313", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:35:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119906856735060038"], "id": "2119906856735060038", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1633874951508721686", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 642, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119864573142749308", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@OpenAIDevs So just to get this straight: You ship to Japan, but drop it in the middle of the night here while I’m asleep. Two hours later it’s sold out, as expected.\n\nMeanwhile, my dot wasn’t even able to buy it for me, even with pre-approval.\n\nReally disappointed!", "url": "https://x.com/MarcelFrommelt/status/2119906856735060038"}, {"author_id": "1522055022422470656", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:35:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119906713751208366"], "id": "2119906713751208366", "in_reply_to_user_id": "384098551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119884573190545726", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_samirism I’d love if my dot could pull things up in the side panel like a webpage using in-app browser or a page/slide etc (this is especially missing with voice)", "url": "https://x.com/maxxrubin_/status/2119906713751208366"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2119906350134378496"]}, "author_id": "1976825482071986176", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:33:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119906353334583378"], "id": "2119906353334583378", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I’m tracking AI weekly usage cuts so you don’t have to:\n\nChatGPT Dots weekly, Nov 2–9: no limit change. Dots can now use GPT-6.1 Terra too, and Enterprise goes live Nov 4 — billing starts Nov 18. Heads-up: shared ChatGPT + Codex allowance lands in December. https://t.co/ytZcZtQj23", "url": "https://x.com/iCame4Grok/status/2119906353334583378"}, {"author_id": "1457145836878458881", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:31:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119905721676689832"], "id": "2119905721676689832", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 60, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "people who convinced me to try grok bot: @poteto, @thecsguy, @jacobgold, a lackluster @OpenAI dots, waitlist for @claudeai duets", "url": "https://x.com/aarondevs/status/2119905721676689832"}, {"author_id": "1973556612662206464", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:21:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119903260559528204"], "id": "2119903260559528204", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI dots can now hit multiple local machines and pick which one runs a task. Build on the laptop, test on another box. Same idea I've been wiring with agents at home.", "url": "https://x.com/AgenticHombre/status/2119903260559528204"}, {"author_id": "1357297713679917062", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:21:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119903146621243554"], "id": "2119903146621243554", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119902335375704330", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @OpenAIDevs my codex cli is on a home server, how do i enable my dot  to send tasks there ? is the an option in the cli for that ?", "url": "https://x.com/flopsy42/status/2119903146621243554"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "16_2119928678159421440", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HWt_5qLbEAAFpno.jpg", "type": "animated_gif"}, {"media_key": "3_2119922037682479104", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWt53IeWIAA3hSd.jpg"}, {"media_key": "3_2119916784027312128", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWt1FVFWIAA259y.jpg"}, {"media_key